  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with 6-phospho-beta-glucosidase BglT through a series of intermediate targets, primarily through Ent-Gloeosteretriol. This suggests a potential pathway where Oblonganoside C may modulate Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn affects BglT. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Oblonganoside C is a target of two different entities, NCI-H1734 and Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK/SBK1, both of which are targets of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which ultimately targets BglT. This implies that the interaction between Oblonganoside C and BglT may be mediated through Ent-Gloeosteretriol, possibly via a regulatory mechanism involving kinase activity or enzyme inhibition. The integration of these paths highlights a possible mechanism where Oblonganoside C influences Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which then modulates BglT, suggesting a role in metabolic or enzymatic regulation. The evidence supports a functional link between Oblonganoside C and BglT through a chain of targets, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
